  "answer": "Windows Terminal can already do this, but only by editing settings.json. The Settings UI doesn't support it yet (tracked in terminal#14475). Set the profile's colorScheme to an object with separate light and dark schemes, for example: \"colorScheme\": { \"light\": \"One Half Light\", \"dark\": \"One Half Dark\" }. The pane colors then follow the Terminal theme. For that, set the app theme (Settings > Appearance > Theme) to 'Use Windows theme'. Docs: learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/terminal/customize-settings/profile-appearance#color-scheme. The older request for a dedicated 'Match System' scheme entry in the UI is covered by terminal#4066. That ticket is the main tracking thread for this request."
